#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Bitcoin block explorer for Umbrel, on your own Bitcoin node (Python standard library only).

One file for both Bitcoin chains: CHAIN=sha256 (the Bitcoin Node app, "Bitcoin Explorer" at btc.hashes.space) or
CHAIN=blake2b (the Bitcoin Knots app on the BLAKE2b chain, "Bitcoin BLAKE2b Explorer" at btcb2.hashes.space).
Reads everything from the node's RPC, pruned or not, and serves:

  /                      the node's state, the latest blocks and the mempool
  /block/<hash|height>   a block with its transactions (a block the pruned node no longer keeps links to mempool.space)
  /tx/<txid>             a transaction (mempool, a block you came from, or any tx with -txindex)
  /search?q=             height, block hash or txid
  /api/v1/blocks         the last blocks, in mempool.space's format, with the fees and the pool worked out from your node
  /api/v1/fees/mempool-blocks   the blocks your mempool would build, best fee rate first
  /api/blocks/tip/height
  /api/v1/mining/hashrate/<period>  global hashrate and difficulty, from the block headers (24h, 14d, 1m, 6m, 1y)
  /api/v1/mining/pools/<period>     blocks per mining pool, from the tags and payout addresses in each coinbase
  /api/v1/ws             mempool.space's WebSocket: {"action":"want","data":["blocks","mempool-blocks"]}
  /api/v1/status         what the explorer sees of the node (for when something does not show up)

Fees are in sat/vB. The explorer refuses to serve (the page then uses mempool.space, or mempool.guide for the BLAKE2b
chain) while the node is still syncing, because a node that is behind would show old blocks as live.
"""

